tomObjectMapper).yamlMapper(customYamlMapper).build()'}], 'expected': 'The resulting factory uses the same ObjectMapper instance (customObjectMapper) and the same YAMLMapper instance (customYamlMapper) as the blueprint.', 'description': 'Ensures that custom mapper objects are not replaced by defaults when cloning via the builder method.'}]}, {'group': 'builder(JsonSchemaFactory) - copies added meta‑schemas', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'blueprint', 'value': 'JsonSchemaFactory built with Builder().addMetaSchema(meta1).addMetaSchema(meta2).build() where meta1.getUri() = "urn:meta:1" and meta2.getUri() = "urn:meta:2"'}], 'expected': 'The new factory contains both meta‑schemas with normalized URIs ("urn:meta:1" and "urn:meta:2") in its jsonMetaSchemas map, matching the blueprint’s collection.', 'description': 'Checks that all meta‑schemas added to the blueprint are duplicated in the cloned factory.'}]}, {'group': 'builder(JsonSchemaFactory) - copies deprecated URI mappings (uriMap)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'blueprint', 'value': 'JsonSchemaFactory built with Builder().addUriMappings(Map.of("http://old.com", "http://new.com")).build()'}], 'expected': 'The cloned factory’s internal uriMap contains the entry "http://old.com" → "http://new.com" exactly as in the blueprint.', 'description': 'Even though addUriMappings is deprecated, the builder method must copy the map from the blueprint.'}]}, {'group': 'builder(JsonSchemaFactory) - copies custom URIFactory mappings', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'blueprint', 'value': 'JsonSchemaFactory built with Builder().uriFactory(customFactory, "custom").build()'}], 'expected': 'The resulting factory’s URIFactory contains a mapping for scheme "custom" that resolves to the same customFactory instance.', 'description': 'Validates that custom scheme‑to‑factory associations are transferred to the new factory.'}]}, {'group': 'builder(JsonSchemaFactory) - copies custom URIFetcher mappings', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'blueprint', 'value': 'JsonSchemaFactory built with Builder().uriFetcher(customFetcher, "custom").build()'}], 'expected': 'The new factory’s URIFetcher holds a mapping for scheme "custom" that points to the same customFetcher instance.', 'description': 'Ensures that custom scheme‑to‑fetcher associations are preserved when cloning.'}]}, {'group': 'builder(JsonSchemaFactory) - copies URITranslators', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'blueprint', 'value': 'JsonSchemaFactory built with Builder().addUriTranslator(translatorA).addUriTranslator(translatorB).build()'}], 'expected': 'The cloned factory’s CompositeURITranslator contains both translatorA and translatorB in the same order.', 'description': 'Checks that all URITranslator objects added to the blueprint are present in the new factory.'}]}, {'group': 'builder(JsonSchemaFactory) - does NOT copy urnFactory or enableUriSchemaCache', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'blueprint', 'value': 'JsonSchemaFactory built with Builder().addUrnFactory(customUrnFactory).enableUriSchemaCache(false).build()'}], 'expected': 'The factory produced by builder(blueprint).build() has urnFactory == null (default) and its internal enableUriSchemaCache flag remains true (the builder’s default).', 'description': 'The builder method intentionally ignores the blueprint’s urnFactory and enableUriSchemaCache settings; this test confirms that the defaults are used instead of the blueprint’s values.'}]}]
